cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Opportunistic In-Band DNS Freshness: DNSSEC-Rooted Reconciliation of Active DNS-Derived Service State over Natural Application Traffic"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-08-26
authors:
  - family-names: Fronemann
    given-names: Marc Nicolai
abstract: >-
  Experimental DNS freshness architecture and Chromium proof of concept in which
  DNSSEC-authorized, incrementally versioned DNS-derived service state is
  reconciled over natural application traffic. DNS remains responsible for
  bootstrap, root trust, recovery, and fallback.
keywords:
  - DNS
  - DNSSEC
  - HTTP/3
  - QUIC
  - Chromium
  - cache freshness
  - state reconciliation
  - distributed systems
